# Real-Time Communication — VTC

Env conventions: `env-development.mdc`. Do not hardcode URLs.

## Two servers (do not mix them up)

| Server | Public URL | Use for |
|--------|------------|---------|
| **Generic realtime relay** | `wss://ws.vtc.com` | Live app updates, games, collab, any non-chat pub/sub |
| **Chat server** | `https://chat.vtc.com` | DMs, group chat, unread counts, typing, chat uploads; **shell bell** live fan-out (`notification:new`) — `shell-notifications.mdc` |

- **`ws.vtc.com`** → the VTC realtime relay — simple Socket.IO room relay (`join-room`, `event`). No MongoDB, no chat REST API.
- **`chat.vtc.com`** → full chat-server (JWT, MongoDB, `new-message`, `/rooms/unread-counts`). Used by **posif-svelte** via `PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL`.

Do **not** add `sockets.posif.com` — `ws.vtc.com` is the canonical public hostname.

## When to use which

| Building | Connect to | Env var |
|----------|------------|---------|
| Next.js app realtime (kanban, newsfeed, games, etc.) | `ws.vtc.com` | `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL` |
| Server-side emit from API routes | Internal relay | `SOCKET_IO_URL` |
| Static Vite app (builder) live updates | `ws.vtc.com` — token on connect, "record changed" pings only | none (address in code) |
| posif-svelte shell / child apps with chat API | `chat.vtc.com` | `PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL` |

**Default for new VTC apps with realtime:** `ws.vtc.com` + rooms. **Never** point app realtime at `chat.vtc.com` unless you are implementing chat.

## Environment variables

Add to `env_development` for local dev. **Production** values for `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_IO_PATH`, `SOCKET_IO_URL`, and `PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL` are **platform-injected** at deploy (`deployment.mdc`) — do not commit in app `.env.production`.

| Variable | Client-safe? | Example (prod) | Purpose |
|----------|--------------|------------------|---------|
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL` | Yes | `wss://ws.vtc.com` | Browser Socket.IO URL |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_IO_PATH` | Yes | `/socket.io` | Socket.IO path (default) |
| `SOCKET_IO_URL` | No — server only | `(platform-injected internal URL)` | API routes emitting to relay (injected; vRack → server1) |
| `PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL` | Yes | `https://chat.vtc.com` | Chat REST API — shell (SvelteKit) and child Next.js apps (`realtime.mdc`) |

Child Next.js apps: read `process.env.PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL`; expose to the client bundle via `env: { PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL: process.env.PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL }` in `next.config` when needed.

Dev (games + LobbyNet — shared relay):

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=https://ws.vtc.com
```

Launch from VTC dev section so `?token=` is in the URL; persist to localStorage; pass JWT on Socket.IO connect (`auth.token`). **No** local ws Docker for day-to-day dev. **No** `dev-secret` or env JWT fallbacks.

Prod server-side emit from API routes may still use internal `SOCKET_IO_URL` (e.g. `the injected internal URL`) — never expose that to the browser.

Expose browser config via `/api/socketio/public` when the client should not read env directly — see reference apps below.

## ws.vtc.com relay API (generic apps)

- **Default namespace only** — connect to `wss://ws.vtc.com`, not `wss://ws.vtc.com/group-123`.
- **Rooms for isolation** — e.g. `group-{groupId}`, `lobby-{id}`, `game-{code}`.
- **Join:** `socket.emit('join-room', roomId)` — `roomId` is a plain string.
- **Structured broadcast:** `socket.emit('event', { roomId, type, payload, echo?: boolean })`.
- **Listen:** `socket.on(type, handler)` for event types your app defines.

```typescript
import { io } from 'socket.io-client'

const socket = io(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL, {
  path: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_IO_PATH || '/socket.io',
  transports: ['websocket', 'polling'],
  auth: { token }, // when your app passes JWT
})

socket.on('connect', () => {
  socket.emit('join-room', `group-${groupId}`)
})
```

Server-side emit from API routes:

```typescript
import { io } from 'socket.io-client'

const socket = io(process.env.SOCKET_IO_URL!, { transports: ['websocket', 'polling'] })
socket.emit('event', { roomId: `group-${groupId}`, type: 'item-updated', payload: data })
```

## Static Vite apps (builder, S3 deploy) — "record changed" pattern

Static apps **may** use `wss://ws.vtc.com` for live updates, on these conditions:

1. **Address in code**: static builds get no injected env. Use `import.meta.env.VITE_WS_URL || 'https://ws.vtc.com'`
   (the template helper `src/lib/live.ts` already does this). Never an internal IP, never `VITE_SOCKET_IO_*`.
2. **Send the user's login token on connect**: `io(url, { auth: { token: getAuthToken() } })`. The relay
   rejects connections without a valid JWT. Signed out → no socket; fall back to polling.
3. **Broadcast only a "record changed" signal**, never the record itself:
   `socket.emit('event', { roomId, type: 'record-changed', payload: { collection, id, kind, at } })`.
   No names, emails, amounts, message text or other fields — any signed-in user can join a room.
4. **Re-read through ZAPI** on every signal (`vtcFetch` / collection helpers with the user's token), so
   ZAPI permissions still decide what each user sees.
5. **Rooms** per record set, e.g. `{app}-{entity}-{parentId}` (`resto-orders-{restaurantId}`). Join after `connect`.
6. **Polling fallback**: while not connected, re-read every 15–30 s (visible tab only); slow poll (60 s) when connected.
7. Emit after the ZAPI write succeeds; a failed emit never blocks or fails the write.

```typescript
import { useLiveRecords, emitRecordChanged } from '@/lib/live'

// listener (staff list): re-read on every signal; poll while disconnected
const { connected } = useLiveRecords(`shop-orders-${shopId}`, () => reloadOrders())

// writer: after the ZAPI create/update succeeded
emitRecordChanged(`shop-orders-${shopId}`, { collection: 'shop_orders', id: order.id, kind: 'created' })
```

Reference: `~/apps/resto_new` (`src/lib/orderLive.ts`, `socketEmit.ts`, `useSocketIO.ts`, `components/StaffOrders.tsx`).

## Chat server (posif-svelte only)

Chat uses a **different** protocol — do not reuse ws relay patterns:

- REST + Socket.IO on `PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL`
- Events: `join-room`, `send-message`, `new-message`, etc.
- Headers: `Authorization`, `x-group-id`, `x-network-id`
- Implementation: `posif-svelte` → `src/lib/features/chat/`

**Child apps linking to network chat** (DM with a user) use **shell routes**, not `chat.vtc.com`:

- `/dashboard/chat/with/{userId}` — find/create DM (`userId` = JWT `user_id`)
- `/dashboard/chat/{roomId}` — open existing room

Full contract: `app-integration.mdc` → *Platform chat deep links*. Env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_URL`.

